 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Asymptotically $O(n^2)$ for a volume of size $n^3$. The number of vertices rendered is $O(n)$, and the number of cells touched by an average ray is also $O(n)$ [S2].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the min/max octree. The memory overhead is significantly less than other acceleration structures like kd-trees for large datasets [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Asymptotically $O(n^2)$ for a volume of size $n^3$ [S2]. The number of vertices rendered is $O(n)$, and the number of cells touched by an average ray is also $O(n)$ [S2].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the min/max octree, which consumes much less additional memory for acceleration structures compared to alternatives like kd-trees [S1, unofficial].
